    "description": "JINJIB Co., Ltd. provides recruitment support services in Japan. It offers Job Draft Navi, a job information website for high school graduates; Job Draft Fes, a joint company information session for high school students; Job Draft Career, a career education support service; Job Draft Next, a service that provides courses that supports first-time job seekers and changing jobs; and Job Draft Teacher, a job management system for teachers. The company also engages in the provision of human resource development services, including Rookies Club, a training program for first-year employees who are high school graduates; Leaders Club, a training program for second and third-year high school graduates who are in a position to mentor junior colleagues and subordinates; DMU, a training program for working professionals; and CSU, a training program for information management and cybersecurity. In addition, it is involved in human resources support services, such as human resources department pack, interview support, and high school graduate recruitment lab; recruitment agency; and temporary staffing business. The company was founded in 1998 and is headquartered in Osaka, Japan."
